{# What Android's web view leaves out, and the Android app does instead.

   Android System WebView has no navigator.share, and drops a download of a
   blob: or data: URL without a word -- its download listener is handed a
   URL only the page can read. The site uses both: sharePost (post_view.jinja)
   shares a post's link, and the painter and a collaborative session save
   their PNG as a link to a blob clicked with `download`. So on Android the
   page does its half here and hands the app the rest on the bridge
   (app_bridge.jinja):

   share     {title, text}
             Text and links only, for the system's share sheet.
   download  {name, mime, data}
             The file, read by the page, as a data: URL; the app writes it to
             Pictures or Downloads.

   The other apps' web views do both themselves: WKWebView has Web Share and
   WKDownload, and WebView2 has both. A web view that one day has Web Share
   keeps its own. #}
{# The script is frontend/site/polyfills.ts, in chrome.js (theme_head.jinja). #}
<script>if (window.oeeeChrome) window.oeeeChrome.polyfills();</script>
